project web: isolated
  state_dir  ~/.fno/projects/web   (graph, ledger, briefs, agent registry, mail bus)
  The only fno file left in the checkout is .fno/config.toml; session
  state lives in the repo's space.
  NOT isolated: the claude daemon namespace and any codex app-server.
  Those are machine-global and fno does not own them. A session started here
  shares them with your real fleet, so an ambient identity marker crosses this
  boundary as if it were not there.
  mail: this environment has its OWN bus. Your real sessions cannot reach a
  worker here, and a worker here cannot reach them.
